A||N||10||Daleford||88 GT suspension vs 88 Formula||||1||
Z||000000||Daleford||01-10-2001||08:01 AM||||On the question of suspension: what does the 88 GT have, that the 88 Formula doesn't?<BR>Pardon my ignorance, but were these the only two models in 88?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||01-10-2001||08:19 AM||||Nothing. GT & Formula suspension are identical. Only difference was the body. Third model was the Coupe. On that one there were some differences in suspension & options.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||01-10-2001||09:12 PM||||The suspensions are identical except that the formula came with all season tires from the factory and the GT had high performance tires.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||01-10-2001||09:24 PM||||The GT and the formula shared the same suspension and powertrains, which included the 2.8-liter 60-degree v6. The coupe only came with the 2.5-liter four cylinder engine and had no rear anti sway bar like the formula and GT did. The coupe also had softer springs and bushings.<P>Check this site out and let it load before you do anything. <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phoenix||01-11-2001||02:21 PM||||In 88 there were 5 different sets of springs listed.  I put a set of Formula springs in my coupe last fall.  Stock Formula springs are right in the middle of the group for stiffness.  You have to look at the spring codes on the yellow tag of the spring to tell which ones they are.  The best I can tell GT's and Formula's did not have the same stock springs.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||01-11-2001||05:42 PM||||I have the GM brochure and it says the GT and Formula share the Same "WS6 suspension". The only reason I can imagine why the spring’s rates might be heavier for the GT is because the GT is 50 lbs. heavier than a formula.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||01-11-2001||06:05 PM||||I'm not sure about the '88s, but the 85-87s had four different rear and five different front spring rate choices within the WS6 option, and just as many choices without WS6. So just because Formula and GT both have WS6 suspension doesn't necesarily mean they have the same springs. See chart here <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/springs.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/springs.html</A>  . It doesn't show WS6/non WS6 for 88, maybe all 88 WS6s were the same, but I doubt it. Was the 88 coupe available with WS6???<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000007||ray b||01-11-2001||09:03 PM|||| Do you know how to decode the spring rate from the opt. list, last of codes  6xx 7xx 8xx 9xx my formula is  6rd 7rd 8lc 9uc can anyone turn this into lbs.    ray<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||01-11-2001||09:07 PM||||Hey thanks Rockcrawl. I did not know that. I guess I will find out what I have now. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||ray b||01-11-2001||09:51 PM||||checked my ex-4 88auto it came with same c springs(8uc 9uc) as did ws6 formula 5spd.do auto 4 weight same as v6 5spd?||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||01-11-2001||10:40 PM||||I have owned several Formulas and '88 GT's and all have had the same springs......front and rear.  All fronts have been "ARD" and rears have been "PUC".<P>Even the '88 coupe that I'm parting out has "PUC" rear springs......the fronts are different.  I'm not sure of the codes, but I do know the coupe front springs are longer than the Formula/GT.||||reg||1
